{"id":"aa-mergeprof.8","n":"aa-mergeprof","s":"8","src":{"u":{"pkg":"apparmor-utils","ver":"3.0.4-2ubuntu2.5","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/a/apparmor/apparmor-utils_3.0.4-2ubuntu2.5_all.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/aa-mergeprof.8.gz","sha256":"648a48006300355586edf8c6f06fc79f0dbc2daf7a2213694f149032b06c1bc4","date":"2025-08-15","origin":"AppArmor 3.0.4"}},"nopt":{"u":0},"desc":"merge AppArmor security profiles.","u":[["NAME","<p>aa-mergeprof - merge AppArmor security profiles.</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<p><b>aa-mergeprof </b><b><i>file</i></b><b> [</b><b><i>file</i></b><b> ...] [</b><b><i>-d /path/to/profiles</i></b><b>]</b></p>"],["OPTIONS","<p><b>file</b></p>  <pre>   One or more files containing profiles to merge into the profile directory (see -d).\n</pre> <p><b>-d --dir /path/to/profiles</b></p>  <pre>   Specifies the target directory for the merged AppArmor security profile set.\n   Defaults to /etc/apparmor.d.\n</pre>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p><b>aa-mergeprof</b></p>"],["BUGS","<p>If you find any bugs, please report them at &lt;https://gitlab.com/apparmor/apparmor/-/issues&gt;.</p>"],["SEE ALSO","<p><b>apparmor</b>(7), <b>apparmor.d</b>(5), <b>aa_change_hat</b>(2), <b>aa-genprof</b>(1), <b>aa-logprof</b>(1), <b>aa-enforce</b>(1), <b>aa-audit</b>(1), <b>aa-complain</b>(1), <b>aa-disable</b>(1), and &lt;https://wiki.apparmor.net&gt;.</p>"]]}